A||||19||Uaana||Attn: My7Fieros||||1||
Z||000000||Uaana||12-15-2000||04:50 AM||||Just wondering on your take on something.<BR>I was coming home tonight after dropping a friend off (DD) and got pulled over for not signaling. mind you it's 3am no traffic for at least a half mile. and I'm freezing! cop gives me a cite for no seat belt.. Is that to justify the stop? Or a legit cite.<BR>Be honest I don't mind a $53 cite in place of a failure to signal cite "which goes on the record" <BR>But do you guys write cites to make the stop legit?<P>Mind you not cop bashing just wondering<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||zeusrekning||12-15-2000||06:31 AM||||Here in S.C. It is against the law to pull someone over just for a seat belt violation. Our state just had a "Click it or Ticket" campain.Which involved like a couple thousand (don't remeber actual #)check points. Then alot of contreversy got started b/c we were getting pulled over to see if we were wearing our seat belts. <BR>But guess how they fix it?? Make a law saying that they can pull you for seat belt.<BR>south carolina SUCKS. The laws in this state suck, it is like living in a catholic school a lot of the times. Seat belt violation = $20 in my town.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||12-15-2000||06:53 AM||||In RI they can't stop you just for seatbelts but if you're stopped for another reason then they can cite you for seatbelts. Doesn't bother me very much for I always wear mine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||RaeQwan||12-15-2000||08:22 AM||||NC them boys will stop ya in ya own driveway and give you one for a seatbelt hehe.. stupid NC..<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwancfa.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||12-15-2000||10:13 PM||||Laws very from state to state as far as stopping someone for not wearing their seatbelt. It just became that way here that you can stop a vehicle simply for them not wearing theirs.<BR>As far as your stop goes Uanna, they didnt have to write a ticket to justify the stop. I suspect they stopped you for a variety of reasons..namely that it was 3 a.m. and you tend to run a greater chance of getting stopped at that time due to much less traffic and the fact that someones out that late. The no turn signal thing was their p.c. for the stop. What usually happens is (at least what I do) is find a reason (pc) to stop a car (like not using a turn signal)....then using that stop to maybe check for DUI or whatever. The fact that he stopped you at 3 a.m. dosnt really surprise me..the fact that he wrote you for no seat belt does kinda. Guess he needed a ticket. But we dont have to write a ticket to justify a stop. I personally wouldnt have written you (unless you gave me an attitude or something  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )..but everyones different I guess. So....BUCKLE UP!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Joe4x4||12-16-2000||11:47 AM||||Stay out of New Jersey !!!!<P>they just passed a law that they do not need any reason to stop you.<P>If they see that you do not have your seat belt on LOOK OUT.<P>Ask me how I know GOT ONE. <P>:eeks:||||reg||8
Z||000006||KnightRyder31||12-16-2000||12:18 PM||||I think in Michigan if you get pulled over for not having your seatbelt on; you have to pay $50.00 plus court costs.<BR>This is why I wear my seatbelt.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tina||12-16-2000||12:23 PM||||<BR>Chances are they used the NO SIGNAL as an <BR>excuse to pull you over.<BR>Found out you weren't a Drunk on Wheels, and let you go with a NO SEATBELT.<P>BTW as far as I know in Minnesota, can't use no seatbelt to pull you over.<BR>Unless, it is a child not properly restrained<P>Tina<BR>Ex Brookyln Park resident||||reg||1
Z||000008||Old Lar||12-16-2000||01:02 PM||||The last time I got a "ticket" was for having my wipers on, but not my headlights.  (NYS law)  It was one of those days where it was intermittent rain,  not dark and cloudy, forgot the lights...$50 fine. I was out in the middle of nowhere, NY, some hundred miles from home.  Cop must have been having a bad day.||||reg||4
Z||000009||Sndfr||12-16-2000||01:17 PM||||OK, so what's so bad that you guys can't wear your seatbelt? <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/AoErat/uhhuh.gif">  <P>And no, it's not gonna be funny when you say "I like to live on the wild side" so don't try it. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/scorchio/sevil.gif">  <B>Matthew "Whyt Nyte" D.</B>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/scorchio/sgrin.gif">       <BR><B><I>84 SE</B>- automatic, rare Fender Delete option<BR>"Fender gap?  What fender gap?"</I><BR><B>(future owner of a 60's-70's Chevy muscle car)</B><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/ut2/redcap.gif">                <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/ut1/mgwhore.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000010||Uaana||12-16-2000||01:25 PM||||Just to clear up the confusion.<BR>Yes I know I was stopped for "failure to Signal"<BR>And My7 covered my question which was. Do they need to write a ticket. I understand why I was pulled over (3am, no signal, small 2 seat black car) But since I was sober and was actually busy trying to coax some blue stuff from the washers I forgot to buckle up for once. In fact I almost always buckle up getting on the freeway around here.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Standard||12-16-2000||06:07 PM||||Last I heard, the law changed here a a bit ago so they could pull you over for not wearing a seat belt.  I always wear mine... ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Black88GT||12-16-2000||06:16 PM||||I think thats the new trend with state laws.  In MD you can pull someone over for not having a seatbelt. I think its just an easy way to get revenue when it looks like they won't make the yearly budget.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000013||Mi Junk||12-16-2000||06:32 PM||||In Canada you can get stopped for no seat belt, and to top it off the fine is $132 plus points. So I bucklet up be for I even pullout of the driveway. ||||reg||8
Z||000014||Cooter||12-16-2000||07:24 PM||||My way to work takes my through one of the most notorious (sp?) towns for BS traffic stops. I have never had any trouble until last Sunday. It was about 6:00 PM and I was stopped for having a blown headlight. I knew that and I had a new one to put in already, but just have not done it yet. So, I get the third degree:<BR>"If you already have the light, why dont you have it in?- If you have time to be out here riding around, you have time to put the light in. .  . "<BR>But then he starts in on my about my mufflers- "Is that a glasspack on that thing? It is too loud and I dont like the way it sounds"<BR>That really pissed me off, because while we were sitting there some 4x4's went by and they were much louder than my car. I explained that it was not a glass pack, but he still insisted that it was! He kept saying how HE did not like glasspacks. I just did not know that I needed approval from every person on the force before having a new muffler put on.<BR>Anyway- I did not get a ticket, but the smart a$$ "Get that light fixed and put a quite muffler on that thing. Consider this your Verbal Warning." I guess he was bored or something.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||My7Fieros||12-16-2000||07:45 PM||||Gee I love my line of work.....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||fiero56||12-16-2000||09:39 PM||||MY7:<BR><B>Anyway- I did not get a ticket, but the smart a$$ "Get that light fixed and put a quite muffler on that thing. Consider this your Verbal Warning." I guess he was bored or something.</B><BR>What happens if we get pulled over by some smarta$$ and we aren't able to hold our tongues and blurt out a few choice words? Hasn't happend yet, but with time...||||reg||1
Z||000017||My7Fieros||12-16-2000||09:59 PM||||No law against telling a cop what you think (at least not here)...even though I wouldnt recommend it.<BR>All I can say is.."kill 'em with kindness!"...it'll get you far, believe me.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>BTW Cooter, where were you when that happened? Remember, I used to live in Jacksonville..still got some friends on JPD there..just courious.<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 12-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||Cooter||12-16-2000||11:10 PM||||My7- not J'ville, but close! My brother is a policeman, so I know how to act and what not to say (Like- would you like a donut, officer?) I have been stopped for different warnings before, but never to be told that an officer's personal preferance in mufflers would cause me to get a future citation. I guess a bright red sports car, loud mufflers and a teen-ager looking driver are all it takes in that particular town. Anyway, I taught one of the city councilman's kids last year and he said not to worry about- so I am not worried. Keep in mind, there was a sign in front of the church in this town that said, "Beware of the policman on the other side of this sign", and signs in people's yards that say "Watch your speed, they have a new City Hall building to pay for!" I love my daily commute!||||reg||1
Z||000019||KnightRyder31||12-17-2000||12:42 AM||||I like to live on the wild side!!!<BR>Sorry, had to say it...j/k.||||reg||1
